Here is an architectural breakdown, user interface (UI/UX) composition, and visual presentation system tailored for Portfolio X-Ray, designed to score top marks on the Agentverse 2026 criteria (traceable reasoning, risk control, real-world relevance, and technical ambition).

Part 1: System Component Architecture
To move from a concept document to an autonomous multi-agent platform, the system is broken down into 5 core layers:

Code
[ Input & Ingestion ] ➔ [ Data & Quant Engines ] ➔ [ Multi-Agent Intelligence Core ] ➔ [ Monitoring & Memory ] ➔ [ Presentation Layer ]
1. Ingestion & Onboarding Engine
Multimodal OCR / Portfolio Ingestion Agent: Parses brokerage screenshots, PDFs, or CSV exports (resolving tickers, shares, purchase prices, asset classes).

Profile & Risk Calibration Service: Ingests user horizon, net worth capacity, loss tolerance (e.g., maximum acceptable drawdown like "can't afford to lose >15%"), and goals to create a dynamic Investor Context Vector.

2. Quantitative & Analytical Engines (The Ground Truth)
Look-Through Fund Decomposition Engine: Recursively unpacks ETFs and mutual funds into constituent equity/bond holdings and weights (solving the indirect ownership problem).

Statistical Risk Engine: Calculates standard quantitative metrics: Covariance matrices, Dynamic Conditional Correlation (DCC-GARCH or rolling correlations), Value at Risk (Parametric & Historical VaR), Expected Shortfall (CVaR), and Max Drawdown.

Thematic & Factor Exposure Model: Maps assets to macro factors (Interest Rate duration, Inflation beta, Oil sensitivity) and thematic baskets (AI Capex, Cloud, Defense, GLP-1 weight-loss, etc.).

3. The Autonomous Multi-Agent Core (Agentverse Orchestration)
Instead of a single LLM, this runs as a cooperative multi-agent system with traceable logs:

The Lead Investigator Agent: Orchestrates tasks, flags anomalies, and determines where deep-dive calculations are needed.

The Overlap & Factor Specialist Agent: Identifies hidden concentration (e.g., direct NVDA + indirect NVDA through QQQ/SMH).

The Stress-Test & Scenario Agent: Simulates historical shocks (2008 GFC, 2020 COVID, 2022 Fed rate-hike shock) and custom shocks.

The News & Macro Event Impact Agent: Ingests external news/central bank announcements and projects how rate changes or supply shocks ripple through the portfolio's factor betas.

The Risk Auditor & Explainability Agent: Translates quantitative metrics into conversational, jargon-free English while attaching inspectable audit trails (formula, underlying data points, confidence bounds).

4. Continuous Memory & Tracking Engine
Acknowledged Risk Ledger: Tracks which risks the user has already acknowledged (e.g., "I know I have 40% tech, stop nagging me unless it crosses 50%").

Dynamic Drift & Trigger Watcher: Runs scheduled checks against market prices, alerting only when correlation spikes or drift exceeds threshold.

